---
// Author: Ahmad Shaukat
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ahmad Shaukat: principal information security engineer working across CMMC, NIST SP 800-171, ISO 27001, DFIR, SOC operations, DevOps and network engineering."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>
        I am a principal information security engineer. I work as the only security practitioner at a US
        defense contractor, so the controls I build and the evidence behind them are both mine to answer for.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <section class="stack" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <h2 id="how-title" class="section-title">How I work</h2>
        <p>
          I start from the evidence an assessor or an incident responder will ask for, then work back to the
          control that produces it. A control that cannot show its own evidence is a gap, whatever the policy
          says.
        </p>
        <p>
          I prefer changes that can be undone. Hardening that breaks a business process tends to get rolled back
          in a hurry and not reapplied. Rollback plans, before-state backups and report-only phases are part of
          the build, not an afterthought.
        </p>
        <p>
          I write decisions down with their trade-offs. Most security choices in a small business are a
          balance between cost, user friction and risk. The record of why a choice was made is often worth
          more in an assessment than the choice itself.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack" aria-labelledby="now-title">
        <h2 id="now-title" class="section-title">Now and next</h2>
        <p>
          Current work covers a CMMC Level 2 enclave build, a Google Workspace to MS 365 migration with a new
          identity baseline, and an on-prem SIEM and DFIR stack.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also build open-source tooling, starting with
          <a href="/tools/">Win11-Security-Optimizer</a>, and do independent security research under the
          handle {site.handle}.
        </p>
        <p>
          From 2027 I plan to offer fractional security advisory work to small defense industrial base
          contractors.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="exp-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="exp-title">Experience</h2>
        <p>Described by industry. Detail is on LinkedIn.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="facts">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Setting:</th>
            <th scope="col">Role:</th>
            <th scope="col">Work:</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">US defense contractor</th>
            <td>Principal Information Security Engineer, first and only security hire</td>
            <td>Security and compliance program: CMMC Level 1 and Level 2, NIST SP 800-171, DFARS, ISO/IEC 27001:2022. DFIR, SIEM, endpoint baseline, MS 365 migration and identity design.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Managed service provider</th>
            <td>Technical Consultant, SOC operations</td>
            <td>Secureworks Taegis XDR operations across three financial-services client accounts, with oversight of L1 to L3 tiers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Technology services</th>
            <td>DevOps and Network Engineer</td>
            <td>Hardened golden-image pipeline built with Packer, Terraform and Ansible.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Network services provider</th>
            <td>Network Engineer</td>
            <td>Network engineering in telecommunications carrier and data centre environments.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cred-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="cred-title">Education and credentials</h2>
      </div>
      <table class="facts">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Credential:</th>
            <th scope="col">Status:</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Bachelor of Information Technology (Network Security), TAFE NSW</th>
            <td>Completed</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">ISC2 Certified in Cybersecurity</th>
            <td>Exam scheduled, late 2026</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Risk Management Framework (RMF) course</th>
            <td>In progress</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">CISSP</th>
            <td>Planned, 2027</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="tools-title">Working toolset</h2>
      </div>
      <table class="facts">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Area:</th>
            <th scope="col">Tools and standards:</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Compliance</th><td>CMMC 2.0, NIST SP 800-171 Rev 2 and Rev 3, DFARS 252.204-7012, ISO/IEC 27001:2022, ISO 19011 internal audit</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Identity and cloud</th><td>Entra ID Conditional Access, Intune, MS Defender, Exchange Online, Autopilot</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Detection</th><td>Wazuh, Sysmon, TheHive, Cortex, MISP, Secureworks Taegis XDR</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">DFIR</th><td>KAPE, Eric Zimmerman's tools, THOR Lite, Hayabusa, Chainsaw, SIFT</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Endpoint and automation</th><td>Action1 RMM, PowerShell, Packer, Terraform, Ansible</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Network</th><td>OPNsense, Zenarmor, enterprise firewalls in FIPS mode, carrier and data centre routing</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 700;
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
</style>
